course: dictionary
lesson: 13555
title: Imprudence: unwise choices
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Imprudence is a noun. It means not being careful or sensible, and doing things without thinking about the risks. «Ben spent all his birthday money on sweets in one afternoon, and his mum called it imprudence.» His mum's word tells you he did not think ahead about what he would need later.
explain: Look for clue words around the word. «Jake climbed onto the icy roof with no ladder and no helmet.» Words like icy, no ladder and no helmet show the act was risky, so imprudence means taking risks without thinking. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The opposite of imprudence is prudence, which means care and good sense. A prudent person thinks before acting. An imprudent person does not.
fact: Imprudence means not being careful or sensible, doing things without thinking about the risks.
fact: An imprudence is one unwise act, so imprudences is the plural.
fact: Prudence is the opposite of imprudence: it means care and good sense.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad's imprudence with motor-cars brings him trouble, prison and the loss of his home.
fact: Context clues such as «risks», «careless» or «without thinking» can point you to the meaning of imprudence.
exercise: «Ben spent all his birthday money on sweets in one afternoon.» What does this show? | Good luck | *Imprudence, with no thought for later | Prudence, careful saving | Kindness to his friends
exercise: «Jake climbed onto the icy roof with no ladder and no helmet.» Which word fits best to describe this? | *Imprudence | Patience | Prudence | Honesty
exercise: What does imprudence mean? | Careful, sensible planning | *Not being careful, doing things without thinking about the risks | A kind gift for a friend | Sleeping quietly
test: In The Wind in the Willows, what does Toad's imprudence with motor-cars lead to? | A holiday at the seaside | *Trouble, prison and losing his home | Winning a prize | Making new friends at a party
test: Which word is the opposite of imprudence? | Rashness | Carelessness | Foolishness | *Prudence
exam: Which sentence best shows imprudence? | *Lily crossed the busy road without looking | Lily checked the ice before she stepped on it | Lily read the safety sign twice | Lily waited for the green man and held her dad's hand
